🐛 Bug
When I was inferring a scripted transformer model with libtorch c++ on a CPU, everything was ok.
The scripted transformer can also generate the correct result for the first tensor input on a cuda device.
However, when inferring the second tensor input on a cuda device, I got the following error:
terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::runtime_error'
  what():  default_program(22): error: more than one instance of overloaded function "fmod" matches the argument list:
            function "fmod(double, double)"
            function "fmod(float, float)"
            argument types are: (long long, long long)

default_program(24): error: more than one instance of overloaded function "fmod" matches the argument list:
            function "fmod(double, double)"
            function "fmod(float, float)"
            argument types are: (long long, long long)

